{"id":"dca22faafaee72fb","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-nfa-determinization.md","title":"DFA–NFA Language Equivalence","display":"thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence — DFA–NFA Language Equivalence","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-nfa-determinization","aliases":["73-thm-nfa-determinization","73-thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence"],"display":"thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence — DFA–NFA Language Equivalence","depends_on":["[[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]]","[[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-nfa-determinization"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-nfa-determinization</span><span>73-thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence — DFA–NFA Language Equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3b7a967565c86f39\" href=\"?note=3b7a967565c86f39\" title=\"73-df-dfa-language-semantics\">73-df-dfa-language-semantics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1d700ea676b35b73\" href=\"?note=1d700ea676b35b73\" title=\"73-df-nfa-language-semantics\">73-df-nfa-language-semantics</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (alphabet)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(\\cdot)\">\\(L(\\cdot)\\)</span> (automata and accepted languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"3b7a967565c86f39\" href=\"?note=3b7a967565c86f39\" title=\"73-df-dfa-language-semantics\">73-df-dfa-language-semantics</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"1d700ea676b35b73\" href=\"?note=1d700ea676b35b73\" title=\"73-df-nfa-language-semantics\">73-df-nfa-language-semantics</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}dfa\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M\\in\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(M))\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}dfa\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M\\in\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(M))\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For the nontrivial direction, the subset construction uses state set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P(Q)\">\\(\\mathcal P(Q)\\)</span>, initial state <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{q_0\\}\">\\(\\{q_0\\}\\)</span>, transition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\mapsto\\bigcup_{q\\in S}\\delta(q,a)\">\\(S\\mapsto\\bigcup_{q\\in S}\\delta(q,a)\\)</span>, and final subsets meeting <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Conversely, a DFA is an NFA whose transition values are singletons. Induction on word length proves preservation of acceptance.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-dfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"3b7a967565c86f39","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-nfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"1d700ea676b35b73","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"3b7a967565c86f39","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}$ and $L(\\cdot)$ (automata and accepted languages, see [[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]] and [[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-nfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"1d700ea676b35b73","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}$ and $L(\\cdot)$ (automata and accepted languages, see [[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]] and [[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}","display":false},{"tex":"L(\\cdot)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}dfa\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M\\in\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(M))\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathcal P(Q)","display":false},{"tex":"\\{q_0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"S\\mapsto\\bigcup_{q\\in S}\\delta(q,a)","display":false},{"tex":"F","display":false}],"bytes":1203,"backlinks":[{"id":"a2d140de13ec8897","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"c94730370dfe9091","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"fa5a4ce6b6982a00","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"Thompson's structural construction maps each regular expression to an equivalent epsilon-NFA; [[73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination]] and [[73-thm-nfa-determinization]] then give a DFA."}],"outgoing":["3b7a967565c86f39","1d700ea676b35b73"]}